**8. Use *my numbers* to illustrate what happens for every possible value of the two optional arguments of the *range()* function.**


```{r}

# Showing two optional arguments for range.

my_numbers

# Two arguments.

for (remove_na in c(FALSE, TRUE)) {
  for (remove_inf in c(FALSE, TRUE)) {
    
    
    result <- tryCatch(
      range(my_numbers, na.rm = remove_na, finite = remove_inf),
      error = function(e) e
    )
    
    cat(
      "na.rm =", remove_na,
      ", finite =", remove_inf,
      " => range =",
      paste(result, collapse = " "),
      "\n"
    )
  }
}


```


